The repo might be private — it's not showing up in search. But I already have the conversion logic from our past conversations. Let me confirm I have it right:

The problem: Hevy's API accepts weight in kg. If you naively convert lbs → kg and round to normal precision (like nearest 0.5 kg), Hevy displays it back as ugly fractional pounds (134.5 lbs instead of 135 lbs).

The fix you use in 531-maker: convert at **0.001 kg precision** so Hevy round-trips back to clean even lbs:

```typescript
// lbs → kg for Hevy API
function lbsToHevyKg(lbs: number): number {
  return Math.round(lbs * 0.45359237 * 1000) / 1000;
}

// 135 lbs → 61.235 kg → Hevy displays as 135 lbs ✓
// NOT: 135 lbs → 61.5 kg → Hevy displays as 135.6 lbs ✗
```

Is that the logic, or is there more to it? I want to make sure I'm not missing an edge case before I bake it into the spec.
